-- Under the LEST of a MUST, a bare AFTER counts from the failure time, which
-- is the missed deadline (EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC §5.2) — the very instant
-- WITHIN … OF THE DEADLINE names. So AFTER 3 WITHIN 2 OF THE DEADLINE there
-- is [deadline+3, deadline+2]: closes before it opens, refused with both
-- offsets literal (§5.1.2.2). Under a SHANT's LEST the failure time is the
-- violating act's stamp, an earlier instant, and the same literals are not
-- compared (ok/every/run-after.l4, `cure after violation, deadline within`).

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Buyer
    Seller

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Pay
    Deliver

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
bad MEANS
    PARTY Seller MUST Deliver WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST (PARTY Buyer MUST Pay AFTER 3 WITHIN 2 OF THE DEADLINE)
